Title: Test Fountain Script
Credit: Written by
Author: Regression Test
Draft date: 2026-01-01

INT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

A modest coffee shop. Morning light. ALICE (30s, tired) sits across from BOB (40s, alert).

ALICE
You said you'd be on time.

BOB
Traffic was brutal.

ALICE
(skeptical)
Traffic. Right.

Bob shrugs and orders an espresso. Alice studies him.

ALICE (CONT'D)
We need to talk about the deal.

BOB
Now? Here?

ALICE
Yes. Now.

EXT. STREET - LATER

Alice and Bob walk briskly down a busy sidewalk. CARS honk in the background.

BOB
Fine. What's on your mind?

ALICE
The numbers don't add up. I've checked them three times.

BOB (V.O.)
She was right. The numbers never added up.

INT. OFFICE - NIGHT

A cramped office. Papers everywhere. CHARLIE (50s, weary) reviews documents at a desk.

CHARLIE
This is a mess.

Charlie picks up the phone and dials.

CHARLIE (CONT'D)
We have a problem.

FADE OUT.
